# Update the README

`README.md` is only the setup and run process: required tools, install commands, how to start and stop the server, the URL, and the short failure table.

When install steps, run steps, required tools, ports, or the command that serves the page change, update `README.md` in the same turn so a new clone can still install and run from that file alone.

Keep explanations of the course, architecture, and interview material in `docs/`. Do not grow `README.md` into that material.

Do not change application code or run commands as part of a README update unless the user asks for that.
